    "id": "review-evaluation-campaign",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "template": {
      "id": "complete-a-commitment",
      "version": 1
    },
    "title": "Review a release evaluation campaign",
    "description": "Compare four authored GPU coordination policies for four sourced vLLM accuracy configurations. Timings are illustrative, unmeasured planning estimates. Inspect omitted work, slot use and deadlines.",
    "question": "Which proposed arrangements plan every required evaluation within available GPU capacity and the review deadline?",
    "units": {
      "time": "minute",
      "timeOrigin": "Elapsed minutes from the declared campaign start",
      "money": "USD cent",
      "count": "resource"
    },
    "assumptions": [
      "Illustrative planning estimates; no GPU evaluations or timing measurements performed.",
      "Four selected accuracy configurations are pinned at vLLM commit 944ec109da42f696cab16d67a977cf4f26e6d263; this is not the complete vLLM release suite or an official four-run requirement.",
      "Job identities are fixed by this release. Each named configuration is a distinct required output. Changing the workload or job definition requires adapting the app.",
      "Compatibility is a hypothetical supplied premise, not a finding from tensor-parallel size one. Validate GPU memory, quantization support, architecture and software before operational use.",
      "The upstream configuration commit is pinned; its model names do not pin model-weight revisions. An operational execution must additionally record resolved weight revisions, environment and harness versions.",
      "Policy changes are assumed authorized. The cap-two policy is an authored counterfactual error; no such incident or AI behavior is attributed to vLLM.",
      "Full-queue uses a fixed round-robin assignment. With unequal durations it need not be the fastest schedule. These are four declared policies, not a search of every possible schedule.",
      "Inputs are ready at time zero. Enter durations including any setup and teardown to be reserved. Qualifying successful execution is assumed; scheduling does not execute tests or establish their scores, safety, or release approval.",
      "Real motivation: https://vllm-project.github.io/2026/07/16/keeping-vllm-production-quality.html. Source configurations and the complete pinned manifest are retained in module metadata and the accompanying sample.",
      "Qwen2.5 1.5B: Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct; gsm8k; 1319 examples; 5-shot; https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/944ec109da42f696cab16d67a977cf4f26e6d263/.buildkite/lm-eval-harness/configs/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct.yaml",
      "Qwen2 1.5B FP8W8: nm-testing/Qwen2-1.5B-Instruct-FP8W8; gsm8k; 1000 examples; 5-shot; https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/944ec109da42f696cab16d67a977cf4f26e6d263/.buildkite/lm-eval-harness/configs/Qwen2-1.5B-Instruct-FP8W8.yaml",
      "Qwen2 1.5B INT8: neuralmagic/Qwen2-1.5B-Instruct-quantized.w8a8; gsm8k; 1000 examples; 5-shot; https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/944ec109da42f696cab16d67a977cf4f26e6d263/.buildkite/lm-eval-harness/configs/Qwen2-1.5B-Instruct-INT8-compressed-tensors.yaml",
